<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<div class="wrap narrow page legal">
  <% if (user && user.role === 'admin') { %>
    <div class="draft-banner">Draft for review. Get this checked before launch. Only admins see this note.</div>
  <% } %>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated <%= new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-AU', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }) %></p>

  <p>This explains what personal information <%= siteName %> collects, why, and what we do with it. We handle personal information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Everyone:</strong> name, email, mobile number and password (stored encrypted).</li>
    <li><strong>Customers:</strong> job details, photos and the job address.</li>
    <li><strong>Tradies:</strong> business name, ABN, trades, service areas, licence number and insurance details.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments:</strong> handled by Stripe. We never see or store full card or bank account numbers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who sees what</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Job titles, descriptions, photos and the suburb or town are visible to anyone browsing jobs. The full job address is not.</li>
    <li>Your name, phone, email and street address are only shared with the other party once a quote is accepted.</li>
    <li>Tradies' business names, trades, areas, licence numbers and reviews appear on their public profile. ABN and insurance details are only seen by us.</li>
    <li>We share information with Stripe to process payments and payouts, and with our hosting provider to run the site. We don't sell your information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>While your account is open, and afterwards for as long as we need to for tax, legal or dispute reasons.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see or correct your information, or to close your account, by emailing <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>. If you're unhappy with how we've handled your information, tell us first. You can also contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use one cookie to keep you logged in. No advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
